      "content": "After a thorough investigation, it has been clarified that the observed anomalies during the 10:14 am duration were not caused by high-frequency latency fluctuations but were instead exceptional events of unconfirmed orders. Analysis of the logic logs confirms that the algorithm's parameters remained consistent throughout the period; however, the execution logic was handling a much larger number of simultaneous order submissions than is typical, as per the default configuration. The system was expectedly overwhelmed, leading to temporary execution inconsistencies. While no deviation in programmed logic was identified, the handling capacity was exceeded. A careful, targeted recalibration during a cooling-off period when market volatility is lower would be most appropriate. By doing so, we retain the opportunity to minimize potential losses compared to a full cessation of operations, considering that the system's baseline stability confirms it should resume operations shortly post-calibration.",
